ROLE: systems_reviewer  VOTE: yellow
PROMPT_VERSION: v001
EXISTING_IMPLEMENTATIONS: [
  {system: "LLMCompiler", url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.04511", overlap: "Direct mechanism overlap: plans a tool-call DAG and dispatches independent function calls in parallel; this kills any claim that parallel tool-call DAG execution itself is new."},
  {system: "LLMCompiler package", url: "https://pypi.org/project/llmcompiler/", overlap: "OSS/package evidence that the mechanism exists outside the paper."},
  {system: "ReWOO", url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.18323", overlap: "Upfront tool/work planning separates reasoning from observations and enables tool scheduling, but not the submitted detector-error correctness bound."},
  {system: "OpenAI function/tool calling", url: "https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/function-calling", overlap: "API returns arrays of tool_calls, supporting multiple function calls in one model turn; execution/dependency safety is left to the application."},
  {system: "Anthropic parallel tool use", url: "https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/agents-and-tools/tool-use/implement-tool-use", overlap: "Shipping model/API support for parallel tool use; not a detector-error correctness analysis."},
  {system: "vLLM tool calling", url: "https://docs.vllm.ai/en/stable/features/tool_calling/", overlap: "Serving stack supports tool calling and documents model-specific parallel function-call support; docs state callers handle tool calls in application logic, so no DAG correctness bound."},
  {system: "SGLang Tool Parser", url: "https://docs.sglang.io/docs/advanced_features/tool_parser", overlap: "Serving stack parses function/tool calls and supports OpenAI-compatible tool_choice; overlap is parsing/serving, not dependency-safe parallel agent execution."},
  {system: "LMCache / FlashInfer / TensorRT-LLM", url: "https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache ; https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer ; https://nvidia.github.io/TensorRT-LLM/", overlap: "No material agent-tool dependency mechanism found; these are KV-cache/kernel/inference-serving systems."}
]
CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: insight
SCALE_REALISM: Does not yet hold as a realistic workload claim. The artifact is a constructed corpus with ground-truth DAGs by construction, CPU-only simulation, 4000 steps x 5 seeds, and assumed workload mixes. It supports a conditional characterization, not a population statement about tau-bench/AppWorld/BFCL or production traces. The detector-error bound is analytically useful, but load-bearing real quantities are missing: real multi-tool DAG mix, real dependency detector FN rate e, and real end-to-end correctness under parallel dispatch.
RATIONALE: Yellow because the mechanism is already published/shipping: LLMCompiler is explicitly "An LLM Compiler for Parallel Function Calling" (https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.04511), and vLLM/OpenAI/Anthropic/SGLang expose multiple or parallel tool-call support in current docs. The remaining contribution is not integration-only if framed narrowly as a measurement/characterization: f_indep is reported as a function of workload mix, and f_wrong(e) exposes that at e=0.05 the simulated wrong-step rate is 0.103-0.123, failing the packet's own <=0.05 safety bar. I did not find a prior system in the searched sources that reports this exact detector-false-negative correctness bound, but the evidence is insufficient for green because the corpus is constructed and the scale/workload realism question is explicitly unresolved. Reproducibility is adequate for the L0 simulation if sim.py and CSVs match the packet, but insufficient for the claimed "real multi-tool LLM agent traces" wording.
